57,"breadcrumbIdx":126,"rank":127,"items":-1,"sportId":128,"hasItems":63},"Darts","/betting-tips/Darts/15","betting-tips-Darts","12",15,{"title":130,"url":131,"type":57,"breadcrumbIdx":132,"rank":133,"items":-1,"sportId":20,"hasItems":63},"Rugby Union","/betting-tips/Rugby_Union/9","betting-tips-Rugby_Union","14",{"title":135,"url":136,"type":57,"breadcrumbIdx":137,"rank":133,"items":-1,"sportId":19,"hasItems":63},"Rugby League","/betting-tips/Rugby_League/10","betting-tips-Rugby_League",{"title":139,"url":140,"type":57,"breadcrumbIdx":141,"rank":142,"items":-1,"sportId":143,"hasItems":63},"Gaelic Football","/betting-tips/Gaelic_Football/25","betting-tips-Gaelic_Football","20",25,{"title":145,"url":146,"type":57,"breadcrumbIdx":147,"rank":142,"items":-1,"sportId":148,"hasItems":63},"Hurling","/betting-tips/Hurling/26","betting-tips-Hurling",26,{"title":150,"url":151,"type":57,"breadcrumbIdx":152,"rank":153,"items":-1,"sportId":154,"hasItems":63},"Handball","/betting-tips/Handball/20","betting-tips-Handball","49",20,{"title":156,"url":157,"type":57,"breadcrumbIdx":158,"rank":159,"items":-1,"sportId":160,"hasItems":63},"Volleyball","/betting-tips/Volleyball/21","betting-tips-Volleyball","50",21,[162],{"title":135,"url":136,"type":57,"breadcrumbIdx":137,"parentSport":19},["Map",164,-1,165,-1],"tips-header","site-takeover",{"sportId":115,"sportName":167,"categoryName":16,"leagueName":16,"eventName":16,"limit":154},"Rugby_League","eba0ff68dd4fda32c96e5d03fb71c5151792992004595:ouk:google-chrome:unknown:126.0.0.0","D",{"take_over_banners":73,"take_over_banners_position_fixed":62,"start":171,"end":172,"_cachedAt":173,"_cacheKey":174,"_flushedByIp":175},"2023-09-11 13:38:19","2026-10-31 08:37:03","2026-10-26T05:10:06.917Z","takeover-banners-settings","10.182.96.9",[177],{"slug":178,"location_id":179},"in-events-list","L1",false,{"content":182},{"sections":183},[184,187,190,193,196,199,202],{"title":185,"sections_content":186},"Super League Tips and Predictions: How to Use Them","\u003Cp>The tips table above shows the most popular Rugby League tips and predictions from our tipsters, covering individual match betting and outright markets such as tournament and Grand Final winners across Super League, the NRL and State of Origin. Selections are ranked by the number of tips received, so the most popular picks appear first.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>Click an event name to open its event page, where every tip and comment for that event is available to read before you decide which Rugby League predictions to follow.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>Alongside each tip, you will see the tipster's comments and their profit or loss to 10-point stakes over the past week, month and year across all of their Rugby League tips.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>Our tipsters make Super League predictions on the match betting and handicap markets, as well as outright markets such as the Grand Final winner. Outright tips can appear well before a competition starts, while match tips are added as fixtures approach.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>The Super League season starts early in the year and runs through to the Grand Final in the autumn, so check back regularly for new Super League betting tips throughout the season.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>To see which tipsters are performing well, visit our \u003Ca href=\"/best-tipsters/Rugby_League/10\">Best Rugby League Tipsters\u003C/a> page.\u003C/p>",{"title":188,"sections_content":189},"Building a Rugby League Accumulator from Our Tips","\u003Cp>Every Rugby League tip on this page shows the latest odds for the selection, so you can see what is on offer before you decide.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>Click 'Add' to put a selection on your betslip. The betslip then compares the odds available from bookmakers for your accumulator (or acca).\u003C/p>\u003Cp>Add as many or as few Rugby League tips as you like. You could also include some \u003Ca href=\"/betting-tips/Rugby_Union/9\">Rugby Union tips\u003C/a> to build a multi-sport accumulator.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>Use the odds comparison table at the top of the page to choose a bookmaker. The betslip at their end will be pre-filled with your selections, so you only need to add your stake before placing the bet.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>Download the \u003Ca href=\"/app\">OLBG app\u003C/a> to follow Rugby League tips from our tipsters on your phone.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>Accumulators combine several selections, so every selection must win for the bet to win, and the more you add, the harder that becomes. Tips are opinions, not guarantees. You must be 18 or over to gamble. Gamble responsibly, only bet what you can afford to lose, and if gambling is causing you concern, support is available from \u003Ca href=\"https://www.gamcare.org.uk\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">GamCare\u003C/a> and \u003Ca href=\"https://www.gambleaware.org\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">GambleAware\u003C/a>.\u003C/p>",{"title":191,"sections_content":192},"Rugby League Tips by Competition","\u003Cp>As well as Super League, our Rugby League tipsters provide tips and predictions on the NRL, the RFL Championship, State of Origin and cup competitions such as the Challenge Cup.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>The NRL (National Rugby League) is Australia's top-flight professional competition. Expect weekly NRL tips through its regular season and finals series, alongside our other Rugby League tips.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>The RFL Championship is the second tier of English rugby league, directly below Super League. Our tipsters provide Championship tips and predictions alongside their Super League and NRL selections, and our Rugby League betting stats compare Championship results with Super League and the NRL, including how often favourites win and how many points matches produce.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>State of Origin is the annual three-match series between New South Wales and Queensland, and our tipsters make State of Origin predictions each year.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>The Challenge Cup is a knockout competition played across the first half of the year, with the final in late spring or early summer. Super League clubs enter at a later round than the Championship and community clubs, and our tipsters provide Challenge Cup tips throughout the tournament, so check back from the early rounds through to the final. Our \u003Ca href=\"/blogs/rugby-league-challenge-cup-preview-trends-analysis\">Challenge Cup preview and trends analysis\u003C/a> cover the format and past results in more detail.\u003C/p>",{"title":194,"sections_content":195},"Rugby League Betting Stats: Super League, Championship and NRL","\u003Cp>These Rugby League betting stats compare Super League, the Championship and the NRL across the last five completed seasons, using results and historical match odds from OLBG's own database. They show how often favourites win, how much difference home advantage makes and how many points matches tend to produce, all useful context when weighing up Rugby League tips and predictions.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>All figures cover regular-season matches only and use the result after 80 minutes, so golden point extra time is not counted. Matches awarded without being played are not included. The favourite is the team with the shorter pre-match odds, or the team for which no odds were offered because its chance of winning was too high. Matches with no odds available are left out of the favourite and price band figures. Past results do not guarantee future outcomes.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>How the competitions compare\u003C/h3>\u003Ctable class=\"table table-bordered table-striped text-left no-branding\" style=\"width: 100%;\">\u003Cthead>\u003Ctr>\u003Cth scope=\"col\">Statistic\u003C/th>\u003Cth scope=\"col\">Super League\u003C/th>\u003Cth scope=\"col\">Championship\u003C/th>\u003Cth scope=\"col\">NRL\u003C/th>\u003C/tr>\u003C/thead>\u003Ctbody>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>Matches analysed\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>836\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>955\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>1,008\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>Matches with a favourite identified\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>836\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>945\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>1,007\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>Home win\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>57.3%\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>52.8%\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>54.1%\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>Away win\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>40.2%\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>45.4%\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>41.6%\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>Level after 80 minutes\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>2.5%\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>1.8%\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>4.4%\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>Favourite win\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>71.3%\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>74.6%\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>63.6%\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>Home favourite win\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>73.9%\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>73.2%\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>65.9%\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>Away favourite win\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>67.0%\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>76.7%\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>60.0%\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>Underdog win\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>26.2%\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>23.6%\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>32.2%\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>Average total points\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>42.0\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>48.3\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>46.0\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>Average margin (points)\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>18.4\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>21.7\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>15.3\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>Decided by 1 to 6 points\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>21.3%\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>20.7%\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>26.0%\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003C/tbody>\u003C/table>\u003Ch3>Favourites by price band\u003C/h3>\u003Ctable class=\"table table-bordered table-striped text-left no-branding\" style=\"width: 100%;\">\u003Cthead>\u003Ctr>\u003Cth scope=\"col\">Favourite's pre-match odds\u003C/th>\u003Cth scope=\"col\">Super League\u003C/th>\u003Cth scope=\"col\">Championship\u003C/th>\u003Cth scope=\"col\">NRL\u003C/th>\u003C/tr>\u003C/thead>\u003Ctbody>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>No odds offered\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Fewer than 30 matches\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>98.1% (52)\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>–\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>Under 1.20\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>83.5% (255)\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>84.3% (413)\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>79.4% (136)\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>1.20 to 1.39\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>73.4% (222)\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>70.3% (239)\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>72.3% (310)\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>1.40 to 1.59\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>68.4% (155)\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>62.9% (140)\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>61.3% (292)\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>1.60 to 1.79\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>52.1% (121)\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>48.1% (77)\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>48.4% (188)\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>1.80 and over\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>49.2% (63)\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Fewer than 30 matches\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>46.9% (81)\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003C/tbody>\u003C/table>\u003Cp>Figures in brackets show the number of matches in each price band. \"No odds offered\" covers matches where the favourite was too short to be priced.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>Total points\u003C/h3>\u003Ctable class=\"table table-bordered table-striped text-left no-branding\" style=\"width: 100%;\">\u003Cthead>\u003Ctr>\u003Cth scope=\"col\">Total points after 80 minutes\u003C/th>\u003Cth scope=\"col\">Super League\u003C/th>\u003Cth scope=\"col\">Championship\u003C/th>\u003Cth scope=\"col\">NRL\u003C/th>\u003C/tr>\u003C/thead>\u003Ctbody>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>Under 30\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>17.7%\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>10.1%\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>10.4%\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>30 to 39\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>26.0%\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>19.2%\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>22.4%\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>40 to 49\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>27.9%\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>27.0%\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>28.3%\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>50 to 59\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>17.3%\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>21.9%\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>20.9%\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>60 or more\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>11.1%\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>21.9%\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>18.0%\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003C/tbody>\u003C/table>\u003Ch3>Winning margins\u003C/h3>\u003Ctable class=\"table table-bordered table-striped text-left no-branding\" style=\"width: 100%;\">\u003Cthead>\u003Ctr>\u003Cth scope=\"col\">Margin after 80 minutes\u003C/th>\u003Cth scope=\"col\">Super League\u003C/th>\u003Cth scope=\"col\">Championship\u003C/th>\u003Cth scope=\"col\">NRL\u003C/th>\u003C/tr>\u003C/thead>\u003Ctbody>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>Level after 80 minutes\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>2.5%\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>1.8%\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>4.4%\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>1 to 6 points\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>21.3%\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>20.7%\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>26.0%\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>7 to 12 points\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>20.6%\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>18.1%\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>19.4%\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>13 to 18 points\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>15.9%\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>15.3%\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>15.4%\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>19 points or more\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>39.7%\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>44.1%\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>34.8%\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003C/tbody>\u003C/table>\u003Cp>Stats cover regular-season matches from the last five completed seasons. Last updated: 14 October 2026.\u003C/p>",{"title":197,"sections_content":198},"Rugby League Betting Previews and Guides","\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Ca href=\"/blogs/rugby-league-world-cup-preview-betting-guide\">Rugby League World Cup preview and betting guide\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Ca href=\"/blogs/super-league-preview-betting-guide\">Super League preview and betting guide\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Ca href=\"/blogs/national-rugby-league-nrl-preview-betting-guide\">NRL preview and betting guide\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Ca href=\"/blogs/rugby-league-challenge-cup-preview-trends-analysis\">Challenge Cup preview and trends analysis\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>\u003Cp>Following Rugby Union as well? Visit our \u003Ca href=\"/betting-tips/Rugby_Union/9\">Rugby Union betting tips\u003C/a> page.\u003C/p>",{"title":200,"sections_content":201},"Rugby League Content: Meet the Author and Editor","\u003Cp>The Rugby League content on this page, including our previews and betting guides, is written by Luke Bradshaw Lee and edited by Darren Brett. The tips themselves come from OLBG's tipsters.\u003C/p>\u003Cdiv class=\"author-box-component mb-8 p-6 bg-olbg-light-blue rounded-md items-center md:items-start justify-center md:justify-start flex flex-col md:flex-row color-bleu  compact\">\u003Ca class=\"rounded-full flex justify-center items-center overflow-hidden w-24 h-24 mb-6 md:mr-6 border-[6px] border-gray-500 border-opacity-25 image-outside\" href=\"/meet-the-experts/luke-bradshaw-lee\">\u003Cpicture>\u003Csource srcset=\"https://olbgimages.co.uk/image-cache?src=https://olbgimages.co.uk/storage/gallery/october-app/uploads/public/649/eca/4c4/649eca4c4e5c2098785434.jpeg&amp;w=80&amp;h=80&amp;zc=1\" media=\"(max-width: 1023px)\"> \u003Csource srcset=\"https://olbgimages.co.uk/image-cache?src=https://olbgimages.co.uk/storage/gallery/october-app/uploads/public/649/eca/4c4/649eca4c4e5c2098785434.jpeg&amp;w=100&amp;h=100&amp;zc=1\" media=\"(min-width: 1024px)\"> \u003Cimg alt=\"Luke Bradshaw Lee\" src=\"https://olbgimages.co.uk/image-cache?src=https://olbgimages.co.uk/storage/gallery/october-app/uploads/public/649/eca/4c4/649eca4c4e5c2098785434.jpeg&amp;w=80&amp;h=80&amp;zc=1\" title=\"Luke Bradshaw Lee\" class=\"w-full h-auto\" width=\"80\" height=\"80\" loading=\"lazy\">\u003C/picture>\u003C/a> \u003Cdiv class=\"flex flex-col flex-1 items-center text-center md:items-start md:text-left\">\u003Cp class=\"text-xl font-bold\">About the author\u003C/p>  \u003Cdiv class=\"mb-2\">Luke Bradshaw Lee writes OLBG's Rugby League and Rugby Union content, including the preview and betting guides for the main competitions, and follows the sport closely year-round.\u003C/div> \u003Cp class=\"mb-0 author-box-info\">- \u003Ca class=\"font-bold underline text-olbg-blue-gray hover:text-olbg-orange\" href=\"/meet-the-experts/luke-bradshaw-lee\">Luke Bradshaw Lee\u003C/a>, - Your Sports Betting Sites 👍\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv class=\"author-box-component mb-8 p-6 bg-[#414a5e] text-white rounded-md items-center md:items-start justify-center md:justify-start flex flex-col md:flex-row color-dark  compact\">\u003Ca class=\"rounded-full flex justify-center items-center overflow-hidden w-24 h-24 mb-6 md:mr-6 border-[6px] border-gray-500 border-opacity-25 image-outside\" href=\"/meet-the-experts/darren-brett\">\u003Cpicture>\u003Csource srcset=\"https://olbgimages.co.uk/image-cache?src=https://olbgimages.co.uk/storage/gallery/october-app/uploads/public/649/ec7/564/649ec7564fbfa346637961.jpeg&amp;w=80&amp;h=80&amp;zc=1\" media=\"(max-width: 1023px)\"> \u003Csource srcset=\"https://olbgimages.co.uk/image-cache?src=https://olbgimages.co.uk/storage/gallery/october-app/uploads/public/649/ec7/564/649ec7564fbfa346637961.jpeg&amp;w=100&amp;h=100&amp;zc=1\" media=\"(min-width: 1024px)\"> \u003Cimg alt=\"Darren Brett\" src=\"https://olbgimages.co.uk/image-cache?src=https://olbgimages.co.uk/storage/gallery/october-app/uploads/public/649/ec7/564/649ec7564fbfa346637961.jpeg&amp;w=80&amp;h=80&amp;zc=1\" title=\"Darren Brett\" class=\"w-full h-auto\" width=\"80\" height=\"80\" loading=\"lazy\">\u003C/picture>\u003C/a> \u003Cdiv class=\"flex flex-col flex-1 items-center text-center md:items-start md:text-left\">\u003Cp class=\"text-xl font-bold\">About the editor\u003C/p>  \u003Cdiv class=\"mb-2\">Darren Brett is OLBG's content editor for rugby. He reviews the page content and preview guides for accuracy and currency, and keeps them updated as competitions and formats change.\u003C/div> \u003Cp class=\"mb-0 author-box-info\">- \u003Ca class=\"font-bold underline text-olbg-blue-gray hover:text-olbg-orange\" href=\"/meet-the-experts/darren-brett\">Darren Brett\u003C/a>, Content Editor\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003C/div>",{"title":203,"sections_content":204},"Rugby League Betting Tips FAQ","\u003Cdiv>\u003Cheader class=\"sct-hdr  \">\u003Ch3 class=\"text-2xl\">\u003Ci class=\"text-2xl i-ui-faq text-olbg-orange\">\u003C/i> FAQ\u003C/h3> \u003Cp class=\"mb-2 text-gray-400 tagline\">Rugby League Betting Tips FAQ\u003C/p>\u003C/header> \u003Cdiv class=\"faq\">\u003Cdiv class=\"flex flex-col gap-0 sm:gap-3 sm:flex-row fq-cnt\">\u003Cul class=\"flex-1 [&amp;&amp;]:p-0 [&amp;&amp;]:m-0 h-rst-ls\">\u003Cli data-faq-card=\"\" class=\"group p-2 px-3 [&amp;&amp;]:mb-3 hover:bg-[#fff6e8] hover:cursor-pointer list-none bg-white border rounded border-c-border-2 shadow-sm faq-crd\" data-num=\"1\">\u003Ch4 class=\"p-0 m-0\">\u003Cbutton type=\"button\" data-faq-toggle=\"\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"flex items-center w-full p-0 m-0 text text-left bg-transparent border-0 qa-title\">\u003Cspan class=\"flex-1 max-md:!text-md max-md:leading-relaxed max-md:pr-10 md:!text-base\">How are Rugby League bets settled if a match goes to golden point?\u003C/span> \u003Ci class=\"i-ui-dropdown-arrow text-olbg-orange group-[.card-opened]:-rotate-90 text-xs\">\u003C/i>\u003C/button>\u003C/h4> \u003Cdiv class=\"hidden group-[.card-opened]:block pb-0 mt-2 mb-0 answer\">\u003Cp>Most bookmakers settle Rugby League match betting on the result after 80 minutes, so a match that is level at full time and then goes to golden point extra time is usually settled as a draw in a three-way market. Some two-way markets can include extra time, and the rules differ between bookmakers, so check the market rules before placing a bet.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>Golden point is used in competitions such as Super League and the NRL. The stats on this page use the result after 80 minutes, in line with three-way match betting.\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003C/li>\u003Cli data-faq-card=\"\" class=\"group p-2 px-3 [&amp;&amp;]:mb-3 hover:bg-[#fff6e8] hover:cursor-pointer list-none bg-white border rounded border-c-border-2 shadow-sm faq-crd\" data-num=\"2\">\u003Ch4 class=\"p-0 m-0\">\u003Cbutton type=\"button\" data-faq-toggle=\"\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"flex items-center w-full p-0 m-0 text text-left bg-transparent border-0 qa-title\">\u003Cspan class=\"flex-1 max-md:!text-md max-md:leading-relaxed max-md:pr-10 md:!text-base\">What is handicap betting in Rugby League?\u003C/span> \u003Ci class=\"i-ui-dropdown-arrow text-olbg-orange group-[.card-opened]:-rotate-90 text-xs\">\u003C/i>\u003C/button>\u003C/h4> \u003Cdiv class=\"hidden group-[.card-opened]:block pb-0 mt-2 mb-0 answer\">\u003Cp>Handicap betting gives one team a points start, or the other team a points deficit, before the match begins. The bet is settled on the final score once the handicap is applied, so a team can lose the match but still win the handicap bet if it loses by fewer points than its start.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>Handicap markets are popular in Rugby League because winning margins are often large, and our tipsters make handicap tips alongside their match betting selections.\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003C/li>\u003Cli data-faq-card=\"\" class=\"group p-2 px-3 [&amp;&amp;]:mb-3 hover:bg-[#fff6e8] hover:cursor-pointer list-none bg-white border rounded border-c-border-2 shadow-sm faq-crd\" data-num=\"3\">\u003Ch4 class=\"p-0 m-0\">\u003Cbutton type=\"button\" data-faq-toggle=\"\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"flex items-center w-full p-0 m-0 text text-left bg-transparent border-0 qa-title\">\u003Cspan class=\"flex-1 max-md:!text-md max-md:leading-relaxed max-md:pr-10 md:!text-base\">Do favourites and home teams usually win in Rugby League?\u003C/span> \u003Ci class=\"i-ui-dropdown-arrow text-olbg-orange group-[.card-opened]:-rotate-90 text-xs\">\u003C/i>\u003C/button>\u003C/h4> \u003Cdiv class=\"hidden group-[.card-opened]:block pb-0 mt-2 mb-0 answer\">\u003Cp>Over the last five completed seasons, favourites have won most regular-season matches in Super League, the Championship and the NRL, and home teams have won more often than away teams in all three. Upsets are more common in the NRL than in Super League or the Championship.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>You can see the figures, including favourite results by price band, in the Rugby League betting stats section above. Past results do not guarantee future outcomes.\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>\u003Cul class=\"flex-1 [&amp;&amp;]:p-0 [&amp;&amp;]:m-0 h-rst-ls\">\u003Cli data-faq-card=\"\" class=\"group p-2 px-3 [&amp;&amp;]:mb-3 hover:bg-[#fff6e8] hover:cursor-pointer list-none bg-white border rounded border-c-border-2 shadow-sm faq-crd\" data-num=\"1\">\u003Ch4 class=\"p-0 m-0\">\u003Cbutton type=\"button\" data-faq-toggle=\"\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"flex items-center w-full p-0 m-0 text text-left bg-transparent border-0 qa-title\">\u003Cspan class=\"flex-1 max-md:!text-md max-md:leading-relaxed max-md:pr-10 md:!text-base\">How many points are scored in a typical Rugby League match?\u003C/span> \u003Ci class=\"i-ui-dropdown-arrow text-olbg-orange group-[.card-opened]:-rotate-90 text-xs\">\u003C/i>\u003C/button>\u003C/h4> \u003Cdiv class=\"hidden group-[.card-opened]:block pb-0 mt-2 mb-0 answer\">\u003Cp>It varies by competition. Over the last five completed seasons, Super League has been the lowest-scoring of the three competitions in our stats, while the Championship has produced the highest scores and the widest winning margins.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>Our Rugby League betting stats show how often matches finish in each total points band and by winning margin. Use them as context when weighing up Rugby League tips and predictions, not as a guide to what will happen next.\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003C/li>\u003Cli data-faq-card=\"\" class=\"group p-2 px-3 [&amp;&amp;]:mb-3 hover:bg-[#fff6e8] hover:cursor-pointer list-none bg-white border rounded border-c-border-2 shadow-sm faq-crd\" data-num=\"2\">\u003Ch4 class=\"p-0 m-0\">\u003Cbutton type=\"button\" data-faq-toggle=\"\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"flex items-center w-full p-0 m-0 text text-left bg-transparent border-0 qa-title\">\u003Cspan class=\"flex-1 max-md:!text-md max-md:leading-relaxed max-md:pr-10 md:!text-base\">What is the difference between Super League, the Championship and the NRL?\u003C/span> \u003Ci class=\"i-ui-dropdown-arrow text-olbg-orange group-[.card-opened]:-rotate-90 text-xs\">\u003C/i>\u003C/button>\u003C/h4> \u003Cdiv class=\"hidden group-[.card-opened]:block pb-0 mt-2 mb-0 answer\">\u003Cp>Super League is the top tier of Rugby League in England and also includes clubs from France. The Championship is the tier below it. The NRL is Australia's top-flight competition and includes a club from New Zealand.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>Each competition has its own season calendar, format and play-offs, so Rugby League tips and predictions can look very different from one to the next. The previews and guides above cover each competition in more detail.\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>\u003C/div>\u003C/div>\u003C/div> \u003Cdiv>\u003Cscript type=\"application/ld+json\">\n        {\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n  \"@type\": \"FAQPage\",\n  \"name\": \"Rugby League Betting Tips FAQ\",\n  \"mainEntity\": [\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \"name\": \"How are Rugby League bets settled if a match goes to golden point?\",\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \"text\": \"Most bookmakers settle Rugby League match betting on the result after 80 minutes, so a match that is level at full time and then goes to golden point extra time is usually settled as a draw in a three-way market. Some two-way markets can include extra time, and the rules differ between bookmakers, so check the market rules before placing a bet.Golden point is used in competitions such as Super League and the NRL. The stats on this page use the result after 80 minutes, in line with three-way match betting.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \"name\": \"What is handicap betting in Rugby League?\",\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \"text\": \"Handicap betting gives one team a points start, or the other team a points deficit, before the match begins. The bet is settled on the final score once the handicap is applied, so a team can lose the match but still win the handicap bet if it loses by fewer points than its start.Handicap markets are popular in Rugby League because winning margins are often large, and our tipsters make handicap tips alongside their match betting selections.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \"name\": \"Do favourites and home teams usually win in Rugby League?\",\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \"text\": \"Over the last five completed seasons, favourites have won most regular-season matches in Super League, the Championship and the NRL, and home teams have won more often than away teams in all three. Upsets are more common in the NRL than in Super League or the Championship.You can see the figures, including favourite results by price band, in the Rugby League betting stats section above. Past results do not guarantee future outcomes.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \"name\": \"How many points are scored in a typical Rugby League match?\",\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \"text\": \"It varies by competition. Over the last five completed seasons, Super League has been the lowest-scoring of the three competitions in our stats, while the Championship has produced the highest scores and the widest winning margins.Our Rugby League betting stats show how often matches finish in each total points band and by winning margin. Use them as context when weighing up Rugby League tips and predictions, not as a guide to what will happen next.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \"name\": \"What is the difference between Super League, the Championship and the NRL?\",\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \"text\": \"Super League is the top tier of Rugby League in England and also includes clubs from France. The Championship is the tier below it. The NRL is Australia's top-flight competition and includes a club from New Zealand.Each competition has its own season calendar, format and play-offs, so Rugby League tips and predictions can look very different from one to the next. The previews and guides above cover each competition in more detail.\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n    \u003C/script>\u003C/div> \n        \u003Cscript>\n            // Wire FAQ card open/close for non-hydrating render() output.\n            (function initFaqCardToggles() {\n                function bind() {\n                    document.querySelectorAll('[data-faq-toggle]').forEach(function (el) {\n                        if (el.getAttribute('data-faq-bound') === '1') return;\n                        el.setAttribute('data-faq-bound', '1');\n                        el.addEventListener('click', function () {\n                            var card = el.closest('[data-faq-card]');\n                            if (!card) return;\n                            var opened = card.classList.toggle('card-opened');\n                            el.setAttribute('aria-expanded', opened ? 'true' : 'false');\n                        });\n                    });\n                }\n                if (document.readyState === 'loading') {\n                    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', bind);\n                } else {\n                    bind();\n                }\n            })();\n        \u003C/script>\n     \u003Cstyle>\n        .dark.is-faq .sct-hdr h3 {\n            color: #fdfdfd;\n        }\n    \u003C/style>","\u003Cscript type='application/ld+json'>{\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n  \"@graph\": [\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\n      \"@id\": \"https://www.olbg.com/betting-tips/Rugby_League/10\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.olbg.com/betting-tips/Rugby_League/10\",\n      \"name\": \"Free Rugby League Betting Tips and Predictions\",\n      \"author\": {\n        \"@type\": \"OnlineBusiness\",\n        \"name\": \"OLBG\",\n        \"alternateName\": \"Online Betting Guide\",\n        \"legalName\": \"Invendium Ltd\",\n        \"url\": \"https://www.olbg.com/\",\n    